# PMJAY Point-of-Denial Advocate — backend environment variables.
# Kept in sync with internal/config/config.go — that file is the source
# of truth for defaults and validation; this file exists so a new
# developer (or a fresh AI-agent session) doesn't have to go read Go
# source just to see what's configurable.
#
# Quickstart: cp .env.example .env, then fill in an API key below for
# whichever LLM_PROVIDER you're using. Every other setting has a
# reasonable default and can be left as-is for local development.

# --- LLM provider selection -------------------------------------------
# One of: anthropic (default), groq, gemini. Determines which of the
# three key/model pairs below is actually used.
LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic

# --- Anthropic (used when LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic) ----------------------
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001

# --- Groq (used when LLM_PROVIDER=groq) --------------------------------
# Groq's free tier works here directly — see internal/extract/README.md.
GROQ_API_KEY=
GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# --- Gemini (used when LLM_PROVIDER=gemini) ----------------------------
# The same key Google AI Studio issues for its free tier works here.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite

# --- Server ------------------------------------------------------------
PORT=8080

# Where FileStore persists case records. The parent directory is
# created automatically if it doesn't exist.
DATA_FILE_PATH=./data/cases.json

# Comma-separated list of origins allowed to call this API from a
# browser (CORS). Must not resolve to an empty list.
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# --- Rate limiting: intake (POST /api/v1/cases) ------------------------
# Intake is the one endpoint that costs money to call — one paid LLM
# request per call — so these are this system's main defense against a
# runaway bill from either a bug or abusive traffic. Both are per
# client IP.
RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=1
RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR=20

# Bounds simultaneous in-flight LLM calls, independent of the per-IP
# limits above — protects against a thundering herd of *different*
# clients overwhelming the provider or exhausting quota in a spike.
MAX_CONCURRENT_LLM=3

# --- Rate limiting: everything else -------------------------------------
# Shared by the case-read, document, and evidence endpoints — no
# per-call LLM cost, so the intake limits above don't apply, but every
# evidence submission still rewrites the whole case store to disk and
# every document fetch regenerates a PDF from scratch, so these aren't
# free to hammer either. Deliberately more generous than intake's
# limits — this exists to bound abuse, not to ration a family's own
# legitimate use of their own case. Both are per client IP.
GENERAL_RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE=20
GENERAL_RATE_LIMIT_PER_HOUR=200

# --- Proxy trust -------------------------------------------------------
# Whether X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP may be believed when identifying a
# client for rate limiting. Leave this false unless the service sits
# behind a reverse proxy that overwrites the header (Caddy, nginx, a
# cloud load balancer). A direct caller can forge these headers, and
# trusting them without a proxy lets one client mint unlimited identities
# and bypass every per-IP limit, including the intake limiter that is
# this system's main LLM cost control.
TRUST_PROXY_HEADERS=false

# --- Case retention ----------------------------------------------------
# Days an untouched case may stay on disk before the hourly purge removes
# it. 30 is long enough for a real dispute and short enough that the
# store does not become an indefinite archive of families' health and
# financial details. Set to 0 only if a separate retention process owns
# deletion (0 disables the purge).
CASE_RETENTION_DAYS=30

# --- Intake timeout ----------------------------------------------------
# Upper bound, in seconds, on one POST /api/v1/cases request including
# the model call. Must be between 5 and 120. Kept below the HTTP server's
# write timeout so a slow provider produces this system's own care-first
# error message instead of a truncated connection.
INTAKE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=45
